I walk further through the market.
There is a shop for household goods there.
I see a beautiful basket there.
I like that basket very much.
I go to the shopkeeper.
"Brother, how much is the price of this basket?" I ask.
He looks at that basket.
"This is a good basket," he says.
"This is eight hundred rupees," he says.
Eight hundred rupees!
That is a high price.
I look at him and smile.
"I don't want this right now, brother," I say.
"It is too expensive."
I put that basket back.
I do not buy that basket.
I walk forward from there.
